+- That sum is built one round at a time by `accumulateUsage`, which adds each token field across its operands, so a turn's reported usage is the arithmetic sum of the rounds that reported ([validated by: sums token fields when both operands are defined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
+- A round that reported no `usage` drops out of the running total from either side of the fold — as the incoming round or as the total so far — so a silent round neither zeroes the sum nor turns it into `NaN` ([validated by: returns the defined side when the first operand is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L35), [validated by: returns the defined side when the second operand is undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L40)).
+- A turn in which no round reported `usage` reports `undefined`, not a zero-filled total ([validated by: returns undefined when both operands are undefined](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L45)).

